EVE Online and CCP
------------------

    © 2014 CCP hf. All rights reserved. "EVE", "EVE Online", "CCP", and all
    related logos and images are trademarks or registered trademarks of
    CCP hf.

Clone Bay is a third-party tool. It is not made, endorsed or supported by
CCP hf., and CCP is not responsible for it or for anything it does.

The program reads and writes the settings files the EVE Online client keeps
on the player's own computer. It also uses two things CCP makes available to
third-party developers under its Developer License Agreement
(https://developers.eveonline.com/license-agreement):

  - The names of ships and structures built into the program come from CCP's
    Static Data Export (https://developers.eveonline.com/static-data). Those
    names are CCP's.
  - Character names, and the names of item types not in that list, are looked
    up from CCP's ESI service (https://esi.evetech.net).


